WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Gross Structural Anatomy of the Kidneys: Cortex, Medulla & Collecting System.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:45.000
The kidneys are retroperitoneal bean-shaped organs extending from vertebral levels T12 to L3, protected by the renal capsule and perinephric fat.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Coronal section shows an outer granular renal cortex and an inner striated medulla composed of 8 to 18 conical renal pyramids.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:35.000
The apex of each pyramid, the renal papilla, empties urine into minor calyces, which coalesce into two to three major calyces.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:02:00.000
The major calyces drain into the funnel-shaped renal pelvis, tapering at the pelviureteric junction (PUJ) to form the ureter.
